# Print / PDF report kit

Directors print HTML → browser “Save as PDF”. **One shared kit** — do not invent a
second PDF library or per-report stylesheet islands.

## SSOT locations

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| Brand, logo SVG, `@page`, shared CSS, `buildReportDocument` | `src/utils/sideActionReportPrint.ts` (extract to `src/features/reports/print/` when splitting) |
| Menu / registry | `reports/reportMenuDefs.ts` + builders (`report-registry.mdc`) |
| Data / counting | Backend reports API — client only formats |

## Required chrome (every new report)

- Use `buildReportDocument(title, bodyHtml, filename, options?)` — never hand-roll `<html>`/`@page`.
- Use `REPORT_LOGO_MARK_SVG` / `reportFooterHtml()` — do not paste a new logo.
- Default paper: **letter portrait**, **0.5in** margins (override only via `pageMargin` / documented dense layouts).
- Support **A4** only as an explicit option that still uses shared CSS tokens — no fork of the whole stylesheet.
- Ink-light: hairlines, zebra rows, no dark full-bleed fills (color + B&W ok).

## Typography (fit without micro-fonts)

| Role | Target | Floor |
|------|--------|-------|
| Title | ~14–16pt | ≥12pt |
| Body / table cell | ~10–11pt | ≥9pt |
| Meta / notes | ~8.5–9pt | ≥8pt |
| Table header | ~8.5pt | ≥8pt |

If content overflows: **fewer columns, tighter padding, page-break sections, or multi-page** — do **not** drop below the floor or scale the whole page with CSS `zoom`/`transform`.

## Standard elements (reuse classes)

Prefer existing kit classes before new ones:

- Header: `.report-header`, `.report-title`, `.report-subtitle`, `.report-meta`, `.report-doc-label`
- Notes: `.report-note`
- Tables: `table.report-table` (+ column helpers `.col-name`, `.col-money`, …)
- Footer: `reportFooterHtml()`
- Page breaks: shared page wrappers already used by payout/brackets/elim — extend those patterns

New visual primitives (charts, score grids, bracket strips) belong in the **shared kit**
as named helpers/CSS — not copy-pasted into one `buildXReportDocument.ts`.

## Forbidden

- New `@page` / logo / brand colors outside the kit file
- Per-builder duplicate `PRINT_CSS` blobs
- Client-side “PDF engines” (jsPDF/pdfkit) unless an ADR explicitly replaces HTML-print
- Putting fetch/build logic into `SideActionReportsMenuModal` (`report-registry.mdc`)
- Inventing counting/lock rules in the builder — format API data only

## When Bob dumps many new reports

1. Clarify paper (letter default vs A4), orientation, and must-fit-one-page vs multi-page  
2. Implement or extend **shared** helpers first  
3. Each report = thin builder calling kit helpers  
4. Smoke: preview → Print → Save as PDF on letter (and A4 if offered)

## Backend companion

Data/counting/pool scope live in `fastapi-backend` (`director-print-reports.mdc`,
`services/side_action_reports/`). FE formats API JSON only — do not invent
payload shapes or counting in the builder.
